<title>UK: UK Labour stresses need for public/private deals.</title>
<headline>UK Labour stresses need for public/private deals.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's main opposition Labour Party said on Friday that public/private partnerships would play &quot;an increasing role&quot; in procuring public services and investment if it came to power after the May 1 election.</p>
<p>In its business manifesto, the party also promised to establish a new public/private task force within the Treasury.</p>
<p>It said this would report to a Treasury minister whose responsibility it would be to drive public/private deals forward.</p>
</text>
